{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And why do you discourage, etc.</b> Meaning: besides the objections, I further complain against you: ״why do you discourage the heart of״ etc. That is, even if your intention were only for the reasons stated in your words, despite all this there is room for one to think that your argument stems from fear of the people of the land. And although you disavow this — for on the contrary, you consider the land as though it were already conquered before Israel — it is possible that this is a stratagem and device to cover over the foreign motive, which is fear of the inhabitants of the land. And these are precisely the words of the spies, who said (Numbers 13:31) that it is stronger than us. And this is what he says: ״Thus did your fathers do,״ etc. Further, he intends to tell them that they should have been sensitive to this suspicion, since the deed of the fathers had already preceded — and what happened, happened, that the Children of Israel feared going up to the land. Therefore there is room to think this very thing, when they see that a portion of the tribes seeks to dwell outside the land." "<b>which HaShem gave to them.</b> He further intends here, counter to what was intended in the saying ״which HaShem smote,״ etc. — to say that the Land has a higher status. He tells them that in any case there is a difference between the Land to which they are coming there and the land that they want, for the Land — HaShem gave to them, whereas the land of Sihon and Og is not included in the land that HaShem gave to Abraham. As it is taught (Sifrei Devarim 309), and this is their language: ״לָתֶת לְךָ״ — this excludes the trans-Jordan, which you took on your own. And although this reasoning is the position of Rabbi Shimon, while the first Tanna derives a different exposition, from Rabbi Shimon the first Tanna may be heard, for from the silence [of the first Tanna] they do not disagree on the fundamental matter — whether the land of Sihon and Og is included in what HaShem gave to Abraham or not." "<b>Furthermore,</b> we find that our Sages of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah, chapter 7) in the matter of the ten sanctities, that the trans-Jordan is not fit for the Temple and for the dwelling of the Shekhinah, and thus the verse states (Joshua 22:19): ״if the land of your possession is impure״ — you have thus learned that there is a difference between the land of Sihon and Og and the Land of Israel. And it is possible that for this reason it was not in Moses' mind to apportion it to the tribes, and he desired that all Israel be in the land which HaShem gave them, for it is holier. And see in parashat Devarim (Deuteronomy 3:13) at the verse ״that one shall be called the land of Rephaim.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:38.886435788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}